it, it is much more satisfying to play through the game for the first time and learn these,

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:05.680
learn these spells from the context of what's going on around you.

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:09.360
And, you know, sometimes people will, I think normally it's just people telling you what

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:12.740
it is or you'll find you can, there's a scroll that will tell you things.

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:17.580
But if you know that you can buy that, you can just automatically get the new spells, but

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.680
also you can like hear it from NPCs.

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:22.940
Like this is the spell that you got to go into your inventory and spell it out with the

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:25.060
different runes that each have a different sound.

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:29.620
But I think what's cool about it there is then like, yeah, if you're playing again, then

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:35.560
it's like, well, why not? I, I, as the player did already like quote unquote earn this knowledge.

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:39.960
So now I do feel like even at the beginning of the game, I've started out more powerful

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:45.400
than I would have, uh, on my first play through where I think if you, if you use the guide to

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:50.700
go quite that far, I think it just like robs a little, like the last little bit of like

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:56.140
where the intrigue and imagination and like the fun comes from, from what this system is

00:16:56.140 --> 00:16:59.040
building. It's almost like at that point, what's the point now?

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:04.640
Oh, it's just a chore. You got to just go in and type in all these spells rather than, you know, you know, you

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:08.420
know, you find one, you got to type it in every, you know, every once in a while and there's

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:09.300
long breaks between them.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:15.540
It's not a big deal, but, um, but I really, really liked the, the spell crafting system.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:19.040
And I think it works decently well in this game.

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:24.020
I, I, I have some thoughts about how I think this game could have been designed better around

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:27.540
that, but, but I appreciate this is something I've never seen before.

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:32.600
And, and yeah, to, to sum up what you were saying there, Joe, to, or maybe to put a button

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:38.740
on it, uh, it is one of those things where, uh, you might as well just use game genie then,

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:43.240
right? Exactly. Like if you're going to just give yourself all the most powerful spells, why not just

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:47.140
also make it so you don't take damage at all in the game, right?

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:51.640
Uh, that's what debugging is for, not for playing an actual video game.

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:54.760
So I think we're both on the same page that we don't condone that, but I think it is interesting

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:58.160
that they give you the option for it for like, like a new game plus or something.

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:02.420
Yeah. You just go in and you're like, yep, this time I have a ring of fireballs around me.

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:07.960
Uh, granted there is a workaround for that in the game too, that, uh, casting a spell

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:12.400
that is level four, uh, requires a certain amount of mana that you don't have the experience

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:16.500
for yet. And so you can't just continuously spam these level four spells.

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:19.100
You probably have enough mana at the beginning of the game to do one of them.

00:18:19.100 --> 00:18:24.840
Yeah. Every spell has, once you have the spell, you have levels one through four of that spell.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:28.420
Right, right. So you can always use a lower version of that spell.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:32.440
And for the attack spells, you know, they obviously do different power levels and everything.

00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:37.540
And then I, I think for a lot of the like, um, spells that are, that, that do stuff to

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:41.320
the environment, I think that there are some times where you just need to know what level

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:42.240
to use.

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:47.220
Like there are different, I know with like flying, cause there's a flight spell, like

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:49.600
higher levels, just let the spell last longer.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:53.460
And sometimes it's like, well, if you use too low of a spell, you're just going to fall

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:55.900
to your death in the middle of whatever you're trying to fly over.

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:59.820
Which is weird cause you don't know how long it is to fly over.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:05.200
Right. Which like encourages me to always use flight level four, which wastes some mana.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:08.000
And I guess maybe that's the risk reward that they're trying to go for.

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:11.820
Like, do you want to take the risk and try level two and how far do you think you got

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:15.120
to go? But you know, yeah, usually you can't see that far ahead of you on the screen anyways.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:21.840
So, um, you know, it seems like an idea that wasn't fully baked into the gameplay, but I

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:27.100
think with the, the runes in general, or I'm sorry, the spells in general, like I do love

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:32.880
the system. I just wish that the way you discover these spells, there was a little more variety in them.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:36.800
Like, like maybe have an enemy that shouts the spell as it shoots something at you or

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:40.100
like, and then you got to just see it on screen and be like, Oh, I wonder if I can do that

00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:40.960
spell type it in.

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:42.020
And like, that's a cool moment.

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:43.380
Maybe there's a little puzzle.

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:47.060
Maybe, you know, this is, this is getting a little crazy here for what this game is.

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:50.120
Maybe there's a optional path you can go on.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:52.360
Maybe there's a cave you can go in, but you can also miss.

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:57.820
And then inside there, there's, you know, the, the rune, the, the spell is written somewhere.

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:05.240
Things like that. Like, I think that that is one of, uh, one of the things I think would have helped this

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:06.320
system. I've got more.

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:07.960
I'll sprinkle them in throughout the episode.

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:08.960
Oh, love it.

