00:22:34.240 --> 00:22:35.520
Like they really go all out.

00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:38.260
That's really cool. Yep. And this game goes all out too.

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:39.900
Uh, not just on the magic system.

00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:45.100
It's also, uh, a little, it has a survival, uh, simulator mechanic to it too.

00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:52.220
Uh, because you don't just have a health bar, you have, uh, a food bar, a water bar,

00:22:52.560 --> 00:22:57.580
a mana bar, a venom meter, all of these things that you have to manage.

00:22:57.580 --> 00:23:02.820
And specifically on the food and water, that is a ticking, uh, I mean, just like humans,

00:23:02.960 --> 00:23:05.220
right? It's just like we have to do every day.

00:23:05.460 --> 00:23:09.020
It's ticking downwards and you do have to replenish that.

00:23:09.140 --> 00:23:12.860
And that's why you have to know how much meat, uh, to buy.

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:17.920
And, uh, as Joe concluded, the correct answer is always just have the most.

00:23:17.920 --> 00:23:21.360
If you can, if you can afford all the vegetables, buy all the vegetables.

00:23:21.980 --> 00:23:29.580
Yeah. Um, yeah, this is like one of those things where I think the, the idea of it sounds interesting.

00:23:29.740 --> 00:23:32.880
I mean, I, I doubt anyone listening is like, oh yeah, that that's what I want in any of

00:23:32.880 --> 00:23:36.860
my video games. But like, I think just in a vacuum, if you're not, if you're just making a video game for

00:23:36.860 --> 00:23:42.380
the first time, that idea sounds interesting, but yeah, it becomes a bit of a chore.

00:23:42.380 --> 00:23:52.100
I, I do think like, I think there was a time where I could have found this more interesting,

00:23:52.100 --> 00:23:56.940
where I could have been like, you know, it, when I was just, when I just had an NES and

00:23:56.940 --> 00:23:59.680
like, this is, you know, I only had a few games to choose from.

00:24:00.100 --> 00:24:03.940
Like, I feel like I could have been like, oh, okay, this is like a totally different type

00:24:03.940 --> 00:24:08.040
of adventure where it's all about managing things as I walked through it and whatnot.

00:24:08.040 --> 00:24:13.040
And I think that the food management and the water management and like the poison meter

00:24:13.040 --> 00:24:19.380
and all that, like that stuff would lend itself to a different type of satisfaction as I got

00:24:19.380 --> 00:24:22.200
through the game where I'm like, okay, I'm getting through it and I, and I gotta constantly

00:24:22.200 --> 00:24:24.240
be managing it. And it's just a different way.

00:24:24.340 --> 00:24:29.200
But I do think like that time has passed because of how much video games have evolved.

00:24:29.480 --> 00:24:34.000
It's really hard to go back to something like this and appreciate it in the way that

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:40.140
I, I suspect I could have, uh, if I played it when, you know, when I didn't have a PS5.

00:24:40.580 --> 00:24:45.820
It's, it is a novel idea, uh, even back then to, to have like the idea of like, yeah, this

00:24:45.820 --> 00:24:47.620
guy is, you know, he does need to eat.

00:24:47.720 --> 00:24:48.580
He does need to drink.

00:24:48.600 --> 00:24:55.120
But the problem is, um, specifically, uh, even, even when the games are this early on,

00:24:55.120 --> 00:25:00.280
uh, not even nowadays, but like, if you're going to put systems like that in place, you

00:25:00.660 --> 00:25:04.420
might as well just sell the whole survival sim idea too.

